chip y8950
clock 3579545
samples 24000
mem adpcm-b y8950.bin
# The wrap at the limit address: Y8950 does not reach ADPCM-B's limit
# register (0x13 and 0x14 go to the FM side), so it stays wide open at
# 0xffff, and a sample that starts in the last unit wraps to address 0
# after the unit's last byte, as at_limit() has it. The bytes past the
# image read as 0.
# The image y8950.bin (written by tests/adpcm.rs): 1 KB segments at 0x000
# (a sine), 0x400 (a ramp), 0x800 (noise) and 0xc00 (a square loud enough
# to clamp), then a 4 KB chirp at 0x1000. In RAM with 1-bit access (0x08
# bits 0-1 clear) an address unit is 4 bytes, in ROM or 8-bit RAM 32 bytes.
# Register 0x07 is ADPCM-B's control (0x80 start, 0x40 record, 0x20
# external memory, 0x10 repeat, 0x08 speaker off, 0x01 reset), 0x09-0x0c
# the start and end, 0x0f the data, 0x10-0x11 delta-N, 0x12 the level.
# The status read (offset 0) shows 0x08 BRDY, 0x10 EOS and 0x01 playing.
0 w 0 13 1 00 0 14 1 00  # not the limit on the Y8950
0 w 0 08 1 00
0 w 0 09 1 fe 0 0a 1 ff 0 0b 1 ff 0 0c 1 00  # 0x3fff8: 8 bytes before the wrap
0 w 0 10 1 00 0 11 1 c0
0 w 0 12 1 ff 0 07 1 a0
1 r 0
20 r 0
3000 r 0
3200 r 0
6000 w 0 08 1 01  # ROM: 0x1fffe0, 32 bytes before the wrap
6000 w 0 09 1 ff 0 0a 1 ff 0 0b 1 1f 0 0c 1 00
6000 w 0 07 1 a0
9000 r 0
12000 w 0 08 1 01
12000 w 0 09 1 ff 0 0a 1 ff 0 0b 1 03 0 0c 1 00  # repeating across the wrap
12000 w 0 10 1 ff 0 11 1 ff
12000 w 0 07 1 b0
12500 r 0
13000 r 0
18000 r 0
20000 w 0 07 1 00
